<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eastern Europe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> is the eastern part of the European continent, including the plains between the Baltic, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> and the Urals. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a> dominated much of its south-eastern steppe and trade routes, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> conquered the Rus' principalities and raided deep into the region in the thirteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eastern-europe.jpg" alt="Eastern Europe" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Przemek Pietrak · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_Europe_from_space.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
